Yes — sign it. But reframe what it is: **MultiSend isn't a module you're choosing for your process** — it's not a swap venue or an execution destination. It's a core Safe utility contract that batches several calls into one atomic transaction. What the wizard is actually setting up is a **transaction unwrapper**: a pre-processing adapter so the Roles Modifier can see _inside_ a MultiSend-wrapped call and scope each sub-call individually, instead of treating the whole batch as one opaque blob.

Why you need this regardless of which aggregator you end up using: most swap flows bundle `approve()` + the actual swap/order-signing call into a single atomic MultiSend transaction (so the user doesn't need two separate signatures). Without an unwrapper registered, your role would either reject any MultiSend-wrapped call outright, or — worse in a badly configured setup — evaluate permissions against the wrong thing. Registering the unwrapper doesn't grant any new permission by itself; it only lets your per-call scoping (target/function/parameter conditions) keep working correctly when a call arrives batched. Accept it.

